me":"topic:gdscript","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2025-03-04T13:17:09Z","updated_at":"2025-03-05T02:35:10Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n\nv4.4.stable.official [4c311cb](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/commit/4c311cbee68c0b66ff8ebb8b0defdd9979dd2a41)\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.stable - Windows 11 (build 26100) - Single-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4060 Laptop GPU (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.7242) - 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i9-13900HX (32 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nIn Godot 4.4 Typed Dictionary, creating a Dictionary with the key of `Script`, works during initialization with values, but not assignment.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nCreate a Dictionary with the type as `Script`. It produces no error.\n```\nvar dic: Dictionary[Script, bool] = {\n    Dic: false\n}\n```\n\nWhereas when trying to assign the `dic`:\n```\ndic[Dic] = false\n```\nIt produces a parse error.\n`Parse Error: Invalid index type \"Dic\" for a base of type \"Dictionary[Script, bool]\".`\n\nHowever, the following works without error.\n```\nvar s: Script = Dic\ndic[s] = false\n```\n\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[dicissue.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19071422/dicissue.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103569/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103569/timeline","performed_via_git